      "Language": "bul",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A hernia is a protrusion of a tissue, structure or part of a organ through the muscular tissue or the membrane by which it is normally contained. Most frequently hernial deffect is seen in anterior abdominal wall. Usually contents of hernial sac are abdominal organs or portion of organs. Hernia is classified according to the operating methods combining with type and grading of hernia. Recent surgical treatment of hernia can be divided in to 3 major groups: 1) Hernioplasty with double breasting techniques ( Bassini, McVay, Schouldice, Halsted). 2) Hernioplasty using tension free techniques (Lichtenstein, Gilbert-Rutkow). 3) Laparoscopic hernioplasty. One day surgery is a diagnostic and operative procedure in hospitalized patients in a single day, without night stay in hospital."},
